  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Statistics &amp; Programme Implementation, National Statistical Office. PLFS monthly bulletin ({PM.long}), quarterly bulletin (to {qLabel(qDates.at(-1))}) and annual reports (to 2023-24), retrieved via the eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>. State and UT unemployment rates (§10) are from the annual reports, 2017-18 to 2023-24, both stopwatches, same vintage. Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli and Daman &amp; Diu report separately to 2019-20 and as one merged UT thereafter; the strip shows the merged series, the archive keeps both. Worker-status composition (§07), earnings by worker status (§08) and the education and age cuts of the unemployment rate (§09) are from the same annual reports: one instrument, agriculture years, never spliced with either bulletin.</p>
        <p>Quarantined cells, all retained in the raw archive: Apr–Jun 2019 urban UR is carried as 21.6, contradicting that quarter's own WPR/LFPR identity (which implies 8.8, matching the published 8.9); and the 2017-18 rural-plus-urban earnings aggregates for regular and self-employed workers, whose implied urban worker weight (0.85 and 0.55) contradicts the stable structure of every later year (0.53–0.62 and 0.19–0.25) while their rural and urban components match the published report. Jan–Mar 2025 was never published in the quarterly bulletin (the design transition to the monthly bulletin). The reports' employment-condition tables, written contracts, paid leave, social security, are listed by the API but its data endpoint fails on them; they are absent here because we do not show what we cannot fetch.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>PLFS figures are final on release. The monthly bulletin (from April 2025) and the quarterly bulletin (urban, from 2018) are separate instruments with separate coverage: shown side by side, never joined.</p>
        <p>Where something is not measured, this guide says "we do not know" rather than inventing a number.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Labour, version 1.3, adds the seven-year annual LFPR plate (§03) and the status-by-gender companion (§07) to v1.2. Next scheduled revision: on release of the July bulletin.</p>
      </div>
